    "final_report": "MOCK: rule-based agent stand-ins; Python calculations are real.\n\nMethod: simple linear regression (one predictor, with intercept)  (data version v1; Python: NumPy centered OLS with intercept; scipy.stats.t slope inference(confidence_level=0.95))\nH0: β1 = 0 versus H1: β1 ≠ 0 (slope of y1 on x1); α = 0.05\n\nn = 11; slope = 0.500 (95% CI 0.233 to 0.767); intercept = 3.000; t(9) = 4.241; p = 0.0022; R-squared = 0.667\nDecision at α = 0.05: reject_H0\n\nRegression diagnostics (screening flags; no automatic record deletion):\nMaximum Cook's distance = 0.489209; screening threshold = 0.363636.\nMaximum leverage = 0.318182; screening threshold = 0.363636.\nKoenker studentized Breusch–Pagan test: LM = 0.655308; p = 0.418221.\nInfluential record IDs: illustrative_03\nHigh-leverage record IDs: none flagged\nDiagnostic warning: Potential influential observations have Cook's distance > 4/n (0.363636): illustrative_03. No observations were excluded automatically.\nDistribution checks (descriptive only, never used to choose the method): [{'check': 'shapiro_wilk', 'variable': 'residuals', 'n': 11, 'shapiro_wilk_p': 0.5455846853413836}, {'check': 'spread_check', 'variable': '|residual| vs fitted value', 'method': 'spearman', 'n': 11, 'spearman_rho': 0.009090909090909092, 'p_value': 0.9788365001441937}]\n\nThe analysis included 11 records. The estimated slope was 0.500 (95% CI 0.233 to 0.767), t(9) = 4.241, p = 0.0022, and R-squared was 0.667. At alpha = 0.05, we reject H0.\n\nLimitations:\n- The slope describes the linear association within the observed range of the predictor and should not be extrapolated beyond it.\n- Random allocation was not established. This analysis describes an association and does not establish causation.\n- Inference is conditional on the stated independent observations and the method's distribution and model assumptions; descriptive checks do not prove these assumptions.\n- Potential influential observations were flagged. The fitted slope may be sensitive to particular records; flagged records were not automatically removed.",
